.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman-list 1  "list "
.SH NAME
dotman\-list \- List the managed files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman list\fR [\fB\-\-porcelain\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the managed files.
.PP
With \-\-porcelain, each record is `<kind>\\t<key>\\0`: a kind word, a tab, the key and a NUL. It carries no source or flags, and the layout is stable for scripts.
.PP
The kind is one of:
  file     a regular file under $HOME; the key is its path relative to $HOME
  symlink  a symbolic link under $HOME, stored as its target
  system   a file outside $HOME, written by `apply \-\-system`; the key is its absolute path
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-porcelain\fR
Print `<kind>\\t<key>\\0` records
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
